"Mage Armor": {
  "index": 1,
  "category": "artifice",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Mage Armor"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "I've figured out a way to create "
        },
        {
          "text": "Mage Armor",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " out of "
        },
        {
          "text": "Infused Silk",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ". When I make and wear a full set it will increase my maximum mana and mana regen due to the runes I put in it, akin to a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Set Bonus",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ". I can also dye it any color I want, including combinations of dyes to make new colors!\n\nIt will also drain the mana from a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Mana Gem Fragment",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " in my inventory, and my own mana after that to "
        },
        {
          "text": "repair itself",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\nIf it does fully break (it is rather brittle), it will become tattered and no longer effective. However, I can take it to a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Runic Anvil",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " and repair it with some "
        },
        {
          "text": "Infused Silk",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " and a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Sorcerous Sewing Kit",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Put the armor on the anvil, the silk on top of that, and activate the anvil with the sewing kit."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
